* text=auto

# ── Executable text must be LF in the WORKING TREE, not just the index ────────
# `* text=auto` normalizes to LF on commit, but a checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF into the working tree - and bash reads the
# working tree, not the index. A CRLF shebang makes `#!/bin/bash\r` an unknown
# interpreter, so every guard script dies with:
#     line 4: $'\r': command not found
#     line 12: syntax error near unexpected token `$'do\r''
# `eol=lf` pins the checkout regardless of the contributor's core.autocrlf.
# ADR-0007 normalized the index and stopped one attribute short (96E-29).
*.sh                           text eol=lf
*.hook                         text eol=lf
*.py                           text eol=lf

# ── Generated files are byte-compared by `xtask --check` ──────────────────────
# The generator emits \n. A CRLF working tree fails that comparison on content
# that is identical, so the drift gate is permanently red on Windows and would
# block every commit once the pre-commit hook is installed (96E-30).
crates/kn9t-server/src/api.rs  text eol=lf
crates/kn9t-tui/src/wire.rs    text eol=lf
API.md                         text eol=lf
schema/generated/**            text eol=lf

# ── Raw bytes: never convert ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fixtures are captured provider bytes, replayed verbatim (R-RPLY-010).
crates/kn9t-provider-replay/fixtures/** -text
